# satz — third-party licences

The Rust crates compiled into the `satz` binary, with the licence text each one
ships. MIT and Apache 2.0 ask a binary redistribution to carry these texts, so this
file travels in every release archive beside `LICENSE` and `NOTICE`.

Generated from `Cargo.lock` by `cargo about` — run
`scripts/update-third-party-licenses.sh` to rewrite it, never an editor. The
material that is not a crate — the provider schema fixture, the fonts satz
typesets with, the control identifiers in the catalogs — is named in `NOTICE`.

